my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
    indented line
normal line
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{'a jumps to the first non-blank character of the marked line},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/mark_jump_quote`

**ma** sets mark 'a'. **'a** jumps to the first non-blank character of the marked line (column 0 for non-indented lines, or the first non-space column for indented lines).

**Keys:** `ma` then `j` then `'a`

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0 (on first space of indented line)
- Line 1: `    indented line`

**after_set_mark.png**
- Mark 'a' set at line 1 (wherever cursor was)
- Cursor at line 1

**after_move_down.png**
- Cursor at line 2, col 0 ("normal line")

**after_quote_a.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 4 (first non-blank character 'i' of "indented")
- **'a** jumped to the line but snapped to first non-blank column
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('ma');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_set_mark');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('j');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_move_down');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys("'a");
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_quote_a');
    },
}
